I also divide the pentagon into $\triangle ABC$, $\triangle ACD$, and $\triangle ADE$, each with base length $s$.
Their respective heights are $AQ$, $AP$, and $AR$, so $[ABCDE]=\frac{s}{2}(AQ+AP+AR)$.
Since $A,O,P$ are collinear and $OP=1$, I have $AP=AO+OP=AO+1$, giving $[ABCDE]=\frac{s}{2}(AO+AQ+AR+1)$.

